\section{Water Balance Model}

The controller estimates the soil water deficit each hour from evapotranspiration and rainfall:

\begin{equation}
D_t = D_{t-1} + ET_c - P_{\mathrm{eff}} - I_t
\end{equation}

Irrigation starts when the deficit exceeds the management allowed depletion, computed from the root-zone depth \texttt{Z\_r} and the available water capacity:

\begin{equation}
\mathrm{MAD} = p \cdot \theta_{AW} \cdot Z_r
\end{equation}

\subsection{Sensor Calibration}

Each probe was calibrated against oven-dried samples; the fitted curve has an R² of 0.97.

\section{Hardware}

\begin{itemize}
\item Microcontroller: low-power ARM Cortex-M0+
\item Radio: LoRa transceiver, 868 MHz
\item Power: 6 W solar panel with a 3.7 V Li-ion cell
\item Actuator: 12 V latching solenoid valve
\end{itemize}

